From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 18:25:55 +0200
Subject: media: gc2145: Report control changes as events

The driver narrows the exposure maximum when the frame rate changes, and
now the digital gain maximum when the analogue gain moves. Neither was
visible to userspace: without the event ops a subscriber is told the
sub-device has nothing to report, so a control panel keeps offering a
range the sensor no longer accepts.

ov5640 already wires these up; do the same here.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c b/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
 #include <linux/regulator/consumer.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-async.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-ctrls.h>
+#include <media/v4l2-event.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-device.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-fwnode.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-subdev.h>
@@ -2938,6 +2939,9 @@ static int gc2145_s_register(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 /* }}} */
 
 static const struct v4l2_subdev_core_ops gc2145_core_ops = {
+	.log_status = v4l2_ctrl_subdev_log_status,
+	.subscribe_event = v4l2_ctrl_subdev_subscribe_event,
+	.unsubscribe_event = v4l2_event_subdev_unsubscribe,
 #ifdef CONFIG_VIDEO_ADV_DEBUG
 	.g_register = gc2145_g_register,
 	.s_register = gc2145_s_register,
@@ -3048,7 +3052,8 @@ static int gc2145_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-	sensor->sd.flags = V4L2_SUBDEV_FL_HAS_DEVNODE;
+	sensor->sd.flags = V4L2_SUBDEV_FL_HAS_DEVNODE |
+			   V4L2_SUBDEV_FL_HAS_EVENTS;
 	sensor->pad.flags = MEDIA_PAD_FL_SOURCE;
 	sensor->sd.entity.function = MEDIA_ENT_F_CAM_SENSOR;
 	ret = media_entity_pads_init(&sensor->sd.entity, 1, &sensor->pad);
-- 
